jobs.description:
Are you looking for a warehouse job in an international team with clear working hours and opportunities to grow? Start as a Warehouse Employee at GXO Logistics in Tilburg. You earn €14.99 gross per hour and receive travel allowance and pension.

You work with clothing and accessories. Depending on your department, you collect, pack, check or move products.

Your tasks can include:

- Picking orders with a scanner;
- Packing and checking products;
- Processing returned items;
- Receiving and storing products;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Keeping your workplace clean and safe.

You will receive training for the tasks in your department. There are also opportunities to learn different warehouse processes.

You work either a fixed morning shift or in two shifts:

- Morning shift: 06:00 to 14:45;
- Afternoon shift: 15:15 to 00:00.

You like active work and enjoy working together with others.

We ask:

- You speak English at B1 level or higher;
- You are physically fit and can stand and walk for longer periods;
- You are available for a fixed morning shift or two-shift schedule;
- You have your own accommodation and transport;
- You can apply for a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG);
- You are available full-time.

Experience in a warehouse is useful, but not listed as a requirement for this job.

As an Fulltime Orderpicker at GXO in Roosendaal, you will start with a gross hourly wage of €14.99, plus shift allowances of up to 50%, meaning your hourly wage can increase to €22.49 per hour. This makes working as an Order Picker / Warehouse Employee especially attractive! You also receive travel expense reimbursement of € 0.25 per kilometer.

In this role, you will pick and check orders, prepare them for shipment and make sure everything leaves the warehouse on time. You will work with a scanner and an electric pallet truck (EPT).

Every day, you will start together with your team during the daily briefing in Roosendaal, conveniently located near Breda, Etten-Leur and Bergen op Zoom. After that, you will get to work: picking orders, wrapping and packing goods, unloading containers and stacking pallets. You will accurately process everything you do in the WMS system.

You will work in a two-shift system:

- 06:00 – 14:45
- 14:45 – 23:30

You can work full-time (40 hours). You are also available to work an average of 2 Saturdays per month.

Thanks to the Logistics Employee, the warehouse runs smoothly and customers receive their orders on time. The GXO location in Roosendaal is easily accessible from Breda, Etten-Leur and Bergen op Zoom.

You are ready for an active job as an Order Picker / Logistics Employee in Roosendaal?

- You are physically fit, comfortable lifting up to 20 kg, and you speak and understand English well;
- You already have experience as an Order Picker, Warehouse Employee or Logistics Employee;
- You are available for 5 days per week, are flexible and don't mind working 2 Saturdays per month;
- An EPT certificate is a plus, but it is not required;
- You enjoy working as part of a team, take initiative and are eager to learn and develop yourself;
- You speak and understand English well;
- You are willing to work in a two-shift system, working times from 06:00 – 14:45 and 14:45 – 23:30.
- You are available to work 2 Saturdays per month.

What will you be doing?
As a Production Employee, you play an important role in the preparation and packaging of food products. Together with your team, you help keep production running efficiently while making sure quality and safety standards are met. Your attention to detail and proactive attitude contribute to a smooth workflow and a well-organized production environment.

Your responsibilities include:

• Packing and preparing finished products so they are ready for shipment;
• Setting up, operating, and monitoring production equipment during the manufacturing process;
• Performing quality checks on products, packaging, and labeling to ensure all requirements are met;
• Keeping the work area clean, tidy, and compliant with hygiene and safety regulations;
• Collaborating with colleagues and supervisors to achieve production goals and meet daily schedules.

